02:02:25.650 --> 02:02:26.710
different set of skills.

02:02:27.800 --> 02:02:32.440
Why could we not fill this through with him through a contract as opposed

02:02:32.440 --> 02:02:33.880
to a special employee agreement?

02:02:34.940 --> 02:02:39.400
So actually started getting into kind of uh federal employment law issues

02:02:39.450 --> 02:02:44.110
um and you know there's been some cases where where we've gone to a company

02:02:44.110 --> 02:02:48.250
and and contracted with them to provide a service and then as that has as

02:02:48.250 --> 02:02:53.130
that has evolved the the particular expert that they provide to us uh ends

02:02:53.130 --> 02:02:54.090
up really.

02:02:54.730 --> 02:02:58.240
You know, in, in all other forms behaving like an employee and under law

02:02:58.240 --> 02:03:00.160
we cannot have that kind of contract.

02:03:00.200 --> 02:03:03.190
That's why in, in some cases we've converted those,

02:03:03.240 --> 02:03:06.710
uh, over to special employee contracts because they cannot,

02:03:07.010 --> 02:03:09.640
uh, they can't behave like an employee but not really be an employee,

02:03:09.760 --> 02:03:09.930
right?

02:03:10.190 --> 02:03:14.540
So a special employee con uh special employee is still an employee,

02:03:14.790 --> 02:03:17.950
you know, so it's, it's just a different way in which we actually fill a

02:03:17.950 --> 02:03:18.500
requirement.

02:03:18.790 --> 02:03:22.460
So you can appoint somebody like myself or one of the department heads.

02:03:22.670 --> 02:03:25.730
You can go out and do a merit-based, you know,

02:03:25.950 --> 02:03:28.590
create an authorization and hire somebody into the merit,

02:03:28.670 --> 02:03:31.990
uh, hiring process, or you can do a special employee contract.

02:03:32.550 --> 02:03:34.680
All three of those are still employees of the city.

02:03:34.780 --> 02:03:37.430
It's just done under a different, uh, under a different mechanism.

02:03:37.900 --> 02:03:40.140
Uh, we've used a special employee contract.

02:03:40.380 --> 02:03:42.140
One is when we want to bring a retiree back.

02:03:42.190 --> 02:03:43.900
That's kind of the mechanism we have to use,

02:03:44.140 --> 02:03:47.150
but they are still performing and and behaving like an employee.

02:03:47.260 --> 02:03:48.330
They're housed here.

02:03:48.540 --> 02:03:51.290
They're responsive to, you know, city employee leadership.

02:03:51.500 --> 02:03:53.980
They're resourced, uh, to perform like employees.

02:03:54.020 --> 02:03:57.770
And so under employment law we can't go out and call them an LLC and contract

02:03:57.770 --> 02:03:58.510
with them that way.

02:03:58.900 --> 02:04:01.860
That didn't basically hide their employment status behind an LLC.

02:04:01.900 --> 02:04:02.780
We're not allowed to do that.

02:04:02.860 --> 02:04:05.290
We have to openly call them an employee.

02:04:05.500 --> 02:04:09.370
It's just we've acquired their services through a special employee contract,

02:04:09.660 --> 02:04:12.410
which also then allows us to terminate that.

02:04:12.580 --> 02:04:14.500
We could a year from now, Chief could decide,

02:04:14.550 --> 02:04:15.940
hey, I don't need that service anymore.

02:04:15.980 --> 02:04:17.180
I'm gonna do it a different way.

02:04:17.470 --> 02:04:21.180
