02:04:21.180 --> 02:04:24.060
perform those duties, and we could go create that position with your,

02:04:24.110 --> 02:04:25.900
with your approval and get the authorization and.

02:04:25.990 --> 02:04:29.850
And and hire somebody through that process they would still be an employee

02:04:29.860 --> 02:04:33.330
just like Lonnie Jones is an employee but under a special employment contract

02:04:33.660 --> 02:04:37.660
uh but that doesn't change the fact that he is still subject to many of

02:04:37.660 --> 02:04:43.060
the aspects of our employment rules just like any other employee is um so

02:04:43.060 --> 02:04:44.570
that's that's kind of the distinction.

02:04:45.000 --> 02:04:47.110
Uh, the, the, the lawyers look at this very,

02:04:47.120 --> 02:04:47.750
very closely.

02:04:48.000 --> 02:04:51.070
Uh, we've had some that we thought we could do through contracting with

02:04:51.070 --> 02:04:53.200
a company, uh, and they've come back and said no,

02:04:53.400 --> 02:04:56.170
that, that actually the service you're getting there equals employment.

02:04:56.240 --> 02:04:57.640
You've got to bring them in as an employee.

02:04:57.720 --> 02:05:00.670
And so that's where we instead bring it to the special employee contract.

02:05:01.040 --> 02:05:02.800
Uh, so that's kind of the difference there.

02:05:03.040 --> 02:05:06.320
Sometimes we can do it the way you ask and sometimes based on the law we

02:05:06.320 --> 02:05:06.750
cannot.

02:05:06.800 --> 02:05:09.430
And so we, uh, we look at each one of those uniquely.

02:05:09.790 --> 02:05:11.870
Uh, to make sure we stay in accordance with the law.

02:05:14.510 --> 02:05:16.660
I totally understand that.

02:05:17.790 --> 02:05:23.990
The contract, I think could be written to uh accommodate what we need um

