yeah, uh, yeah, and, uh, no, you're fine,

02:31:35.200 --> 02:31:37.760
um, and I live in Huntsville, Alabama.

02:31:38.290 --> 02:31:39.270
Floor is yours.

02:31:39.680 --> 02:31:41.370
Alright, good evening, counsel.

02:31:41.690 --> 02:31:44.850
Anyone who tries to get around Huntsville without a vehicle knows the dismal

02:31:44.850 --> 02:31:46.590
state of our pedestrian infrastructure.

02:31:46.920 --> 02:31:49.670
Sidewalks indiruptly, crosswalks are an afterthought.

02:31:49.840 --> 02:31:52.950
Public transit isn't in the budget, and our corridors are engineered for

02:31:52.950 --> 02:31:55.100
vehicle throughput rather than human safety.

02:31:55.550 --> 02:31:57.780
We have built a city for cars rather than people,

02:31:58.100 --> 02:32:01.340
an approach to urban design that is anathema to a thriving community.

02:32:01.760 --> 02:32:04.990
Many in the community often complain to you about our unsafe streets.

02:32:05.190 --> 02:32:07.630
The failure isn't just an urban planning issue.

02:32:07.750 --> 02:32:09.470
It is also a civil liberties issues.

02:32:10.020 --> 02:32:14.160
When a city makes driving the only viable way to participate in daily life

02:32:14.300 --> 02:32:17.280
and then blankets its streets with automated license plate readers,

02:32:17.420 --> 02:32:19.420
it is no longer just monitoring traffic.

02:32:19.660 --> 02:32:21.660
It is trapping its residents in a mandatory,

02:32:21.780 --> 02:32:23.620
unavoidable surveillance dragnet.

02:32:23.780 --> 02:32:25.690
You've heard from me plenty of times on this issue,

02:32:25.860 --> 02:32:28.730
but I feel that I haven't taken enough of an adversarial stance against

02:32:28.730 --> 02:32:29.670
your panoptagon.

02:32:29.980 --> 02:32:33.940
Your surveillance apparatus is unacceptable in part because of your refusal

02:32:33.940 --> 02:32:35.700
to allow meaningful public oversight.

02:32:36.040 --> 02:32:39.920
The city's posture that all ALPR data is exempt from disclosure as police

02:32:39.920 --> 02:32:42.960
investigative data under Alabama law is an administrative fiction.

02:32:43.510 --> 02:32:47.020
The investigative exemption in the Alabama Open Records Act exists to protect

02:32:47.030 --> 02:32:49.910
active cases, witnesses, and tactical intelligence.

02:32:50.110 --> 02:32:52.040
It was never meant to shield the indiscriminate,

02:32:52.150 --> 02:32:55.550
warrantless tracking of every law-abiding resident driving to work or the

02:32:55.550 --> 02:32:56.410
grocery store.

02:32:56.710 --> 02:33:00.300
Reversing the investigative process, collecting everyone's movements first

02:33:00.310 --> 02:33:04.950
and calling it an investigation later does not turn surveillance into a

02:33:04.950 --> 02:33:06.230
protected police file.

02:33:06.430 --> 02:33:09.670
It simply hides a permanent surveillance infrastructure from the taxpayers

02:33:09.670 --> 02:33:10.240
who fund it.

02:33:10.750 --> 02:33:13.870
Equally indefensible is the city's attempt to hide behind the government

02:33:13.870 --> 02:33:17.230
community cloud to manufacture prohibitive public records fees.

02:33:18.020 --> 02:33:21.490
As a federal contractor, I understand how locked down the GCC is.

02:33:21.700 --> 02:33:25.060
It enforces strict CJIS and FedRAM standards for encryption,

02:33:25.420 --> 02:33:27.070
access controls, and data residency.

02:33:27.260 --> 02:33:30.420
What it does not do is require the city to print out physical audit logs

02:33:30.420 --> 02:33:33.620
and bill citizens an absurd amount of money for the privilege of oversight.

02:33:34.000 --> 02:33:37.540
Flock Safety's own software includes built-in administrative dashboards

02:33:37.540 --> 02:33:42.670
capable of exporting audit logs as standard native digital CSV files.

02:33:43.020 --> 02:33:46.580
Weaponizing cloud compliance jargon into to fabricate a labor intensive

02:33:46.580 --> 02:33:48.940
printing process is not a security requirement.

02:33:49.100 --> 02:33:52.900
It is a deliberate barrier designed to price the public out of transparency.

02:33:53.300 --> 02:33:55.810
You have built a city where we have no choice but to drive,

02:33:56.020 --> 02:33:59.800
and now you're losing legal loopholes and technical excuses to keep us from

02:33:59.800 --> 02:34:01.620
seeing how our movements are tracked.

02:34:01.860 --> 02:34:04.420
Huntsville deserves walkable human scale infrastructure,

02:34:04.660 --> 02:34:06.380
not an unaccountable panopticon.

02:34:06.580 --> 02:34:10.140
Release the native digital audit logs in the contracts and take these cameras

02:34:10.140 --> 02:34:10.610
down.

02:34:10.820 --> 02:34:11.860
Privacy is dead.

02:34:12.100 --> 02:34:13.160
Long live privacy.

02:34:15.660 --> 02:34:16.050
Thank you.

02:34:16.150 --> 02:34:18.980
